              Game Programmer Role (Entry - Junior)
            </button>
          </h1>
        </div>

        <div id="collapseOne" class="collapse" aria-labelledby="headingOne" data-bs-parent="#accordion_1">
          <div class="card-body">
            <p>We are developing a 2D puzzle-platformer based around an elemental physics simulation with an environmental narrative. As we finish up our vertical slice, we are seeking <b>a Programmer</b> to join the team as we move into full production.</p>
            <h2 class="text-start">The Role:</h2>
            <p>The game is built in the Godot Engine and utilizes a custom physics backend written in C++. We need Programmers who can work on tasks in Godot (player & enemy state trees, enemy pathfinding, puzzle mechanics, scene & system management) and/or backend tasks (optimization, bug fixing, building & refining API calls). We are looking for someone who has some experience in Godot, and is confident working with minimal mentorship.</p>
            <h2 class="text-start">Requirements:</h2>
            <p>
              • Experience with Godot or 2D game development in an equivalent engine.<br>
              • Experience with Git & version control. <br>
              • Ability to communicate within a group setting and meet deadlines. 
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-start">Nice to Have:</h2>
            <p>
              • Experience with C++.
            </p>
            <h2 class="text-start">Location and Hours:</h2>
            <p>
              • Fully remote, flexible hours. The team is largely in EST. <br>
              • ~10 hours per week.
              </p>
            <h2 class="text-start">Compensation:</h2>
            <p>
              • Revenue share upon release. <br>
              • Portfolio piece. <br>
              • Networking opportunities.
            </p>
            <div class="w-100 d-flex justify-content-center mt-5">
